# tools/overlap_copy_allow.list
#
# Allowlist for tools/overlap_copy_check.py: same-buffer copy calls
# that were audited by hand and are safe by construction. One entry
# per line: file|function|dst-base|src-base (bases as normalized by
# the checker). An entry allows that combination anywhere in the
# file, so line churn never invalidates it; the checker warns about
# entries that stop matching so this list cannot rot.
#
# Every entry below was audited in the e942ee2 sweep. The recurring
# safe patterns are:
#  - LZ-style self-copies with explicit disjoint/periodic-chunk
#    guards (r7z_lzma, encoding_vcdiff, encoding_rlz4, task_patch
#    BPS TARGET_COPY)
#  - copies between provably distinct elements/rows/members of one
#    array or struct (decoder state rotation, dirs[] defaults,
#    channel/grid structs)
#  - single-element shifts in correctly-directed loops (netplay chat,
#    cheat list)
#  - row-duplication at exactly one stride of distance (ntsc_crt,
#    sdl_rs90, ctr_svchax cache flush)
#
# Exact-alias findings (dst text == src text) are never allowlisted;
# fix those with memmove, a staging buffer, or an alias-guarded
# helper instead.
audio/drivers/wiiu_audio.c|memcpy|offsets|offsets
cheevos/cheevos_rvz.c|memcpy|block_hashes|block_hashes
ctr/ctr_svchax.c|memcpy|flush_buffer|flush_buffer
